After ascending a second Valk, it seemed like a good idea to play with
an Elven Wizard next.  I had quite a few false starts, partly because
I don't have the proper early game respect/fear, and partly because I
play Elbereth-less.  Now I've got one who looks very promising -- so
promising that, by the time I made it to the castle wand, I decided
that I would try to keep wishless conduct.

My equipment is incomplete but perhaps sufficient. In the blessed
fireproof department, I have +2 CoMR, +5 gauntlets of dex, and +5
speed boots.  My only other armor is not protected -- a thoroughly
burnt +0 leather helm, and +0 unfixed black dragon scales.  I have "oR
from soko and a bag of holding from elsewhere, and also jumping boots
and a ring of levitation.  I am wearing free action and stealth.

I have a pretty good set of stats right now.  As it stands, I have
330HP from alchemy, 419PW, AC -17, INT 18, WIS 19, and am level 28
(from valley wraiths).  I have a fairly nice collection of spells at
this point, including FoD from getting crowned, magic missile, and
healing, but no polymorph and no create monster.

With reflection and magic resistance, I felt ready enough to have
entered Gehennom, but I'd really like SDSM and a helm of brilliance,
plus scrolls of enchant armor to get my AC up in the -30s (just fixing
dragon mail would get me a good way there, but I'd rather have silver
to free up my amulet slot).  What I'm not sure if is the best way to
get there, and here's where my request for advice comes in.

I completely spent my only magic marker, and have no scrolls of
enchant armor.  I do have one scroll of charging (written before I
knew I was going wishless), one scroll of genocide, and a wand of
polymorph at (2:0).

I have two ideas with the scroll of genocide, and am horribly torn.  I
have no idea which is better.  I could reverse geno silver dragons and
try to get scales.  Their reflection makes them a bit tough, but if I
pick an appropriate area in soko, I should be able to fight them one
at a time.  The other idea is to blessed genocide mimics, to have a
better chance of getting useful tools at Orcus-town.

I am also considering charging my wand of poly, as a lot of items here
could be helpful, but I'd like to reach Orcus-town first, to see if
that's necessary (and if it is, to get more magical tool and armor
polyfodder.)

Any thoughts on the best use of my sole scroll of genocide?  Or are
there are alternate strategies I've missed?



